      "id": "adobe",
      "name": "Adobe",
      "description": "The Adobe Approved Trust List is a program that allows millions of users around the world to create digital signatures that are trusted whenever the signed document is opened in Adobe® Acrobat® or Reader® software. Essentially, both Acrobat and Reader have been programmed to reach out to a web page to periodically download a list of trusted \"root\" digital certificates. Any digital signature created with a credential that can trace a relationship (\"chain\") back to the high-assurance, trustworthy certificates on this list is trusted by Acrobat and Reader.",
